# XCU gencat
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# gencat checked by reading the catalog back with a small C program (catopen
# and catgets, via c17) because the catalog format is unspecified; the tests
# are UNRESOLVED when c17 is unavailable.

assertion  XCU.gencat.001
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       $set selects the set for the following messages, $ lines followed
           by a blank are comments, empty lines are ignored, and every
           message is retrievable by its set and message number.
test       t/001-sets-and-messages.sh

assertion  XCU.gencat.002
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       A $quote character surrounds text so trailing blanks stay, the
           escapes \n \t \\ and \ddd give the named characters, a backslash-
           newline continues a message, and a message with a separator and
           no text is an empty string.
test       t/002-text-escapes.sh

assertion  XCU.gencat.003
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       A second gencat run keeps the old messages, replaces colliding
           numbers, a bare message number deletes that message, and $delset
           removes a whole set.
test       t/003-merge-and-delete.sh

assertion  XCU.gencat.004
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#STDIN
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       A catfile of - writes the catalog to standard output and a
           msgfile of - reads standard input.
test       t/004-dash-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.gencat.005
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       Messages before any $set go to the default set NL_SETD, and
           several msgfile operands are merged into one catalog.
test       t/005-default-set.sh

assertion  XCU.gencat.006
anchor     utilities/gencat.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       A msgfile that cannot be read gives a non-zero exit status.
test       t/006-missing-input.sh
